---
# Template. At cold bootstrap, copy to secrets.sops.yml, fill in, and encrypt:
#
#   cp secrets.sops.yml.example secrets.sops.yml
#   $EDITOR secrets.sops.yml
#   sops -e -i secrets.sops.yml
#
# Identifying, not granting — none of these authorise anything on their own, they just tie the
# repo to a machine. Genuinely powerful values (the Flux deploy key, the cluster age key, the
# Infisical and NetBird credentials) are never committed in any form; they come
# from Proton Pass at runtime, via config/secrets.sops.yaml. The admin SSH *private* key is in
# no store at all — Ansible authenticates with the operator's own ~/.ssh identity rather than
# reading it. See docs/src/conventions/secrets.md.
admin:
  user: opsuser
  ssh_pubkey: "ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIExampleExampleExampleExampleExampleExa"
